  I am no longer listening.

  Instead, my attention is focused on the car that just passed us, which has come to a stop farther down the road.

  The car is military-issue, the same as before, once again with two soldiers sitting in the front. If they turn this way, I'm sure I'll see the same faces.

  And now they do turn. The same faces, as expected, tobacco clenched between grinning teeth.

