  These soulless puppets are not true tsurugi. There is nothing in these husks to inspire awe or fear. Still, their power is undeniable.

  Against one, I might be able to escape, but three is more than I can handle.

  One of the two dragoons to my front is speaking to the fallen soldiers, who are pointing at me and babbling in their foreign tongue.

